{"title":"Career roadmap · Quality Engineer","role":"Quality Engineer","summary":"A Quality Engineer in the automobile industry ensures that vehicle components, assemblies and manufacturing processes consistently meet engineering specifications, safety requirements, customer expectations and applicable standards.","facts":{},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[{"period":"2026–2030","question":"What can I enter now?","output":"Quality/production intern, QA trainee, inspection or testing engineer"},{"period":"2030–2035","question":"How should I specialise?","output":"Manufacturing quality, supplier quality, vehicle quality, EV quality or process quality"},{"period":"2035–2040","question":"How should I evolve?","output":"Senior Quality Engineer, Quality Specialist, Supplier Quality Lead or Quality Manager"},{"period":"2040–2046","question":"How can I remain relevant?","output":"Quality Manager, Automotive Quality Head, Reliability/Quality Architect or Continuous Improvement Leader"}],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"For an Automobile Engineering graduate, this is a directly aligned career path. The role combines automotive engineering with quality control, inspection, testing, statistical analysis, root-cause analysis and continuous improvement."},{"type":"p","text":"Typical areas include automotive components, powertrain, EVs, body systems, chassis, manufacturing, supplier quality and vehicle validation."}]},{"heading":"What to build each year","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Year","Build this","Key skills","Proof of progress"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Engineering + manufacturing foundation"},{"text":"Mathematics, mechanics, materials, manufacturing, basic statistics"},{"text":"Complete dimensional inspection and manufacturing exercises"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Automotive systems + quality fundamentals"},{"text":"IC engines, vehicle systems, metrology, tolerances, materials"},{"text":"Per